# The README grid (readme-grid.keys), its cards carrying the SUMMARY lines session-summary.setup.sh adds.
#
# The pane edge is dragged up right after the first launch — the grab zone is the grid row over
# the pane's rule — so every later session is spawned into the taller pane and its transcript
# fits. An F12 (unbound, 0.6 s) after each launch and each project open lets it settle before the
# next key (a `p` pressed while a launch is still landing is lost and the task types as hotkeys),
# and the run of them at the end lets the PR sweep and the delayed finishes land. The stand-in's
# unread finishes are posted 10–16 s after their launch, once the keys have moved on; about one run
# in three the grid switches itself onto relay-cli while they land (see the footer: it should read
# `orbit-api ▸ feat/auth-tokens ▸ …`) — rerun the scene when it does.
